                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24d5c569-b782-4be5-9e26-c19efa593a4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "3b90d5c2-5cab-30fd-bf86-32682586d6b9",
                        "source_sense_id": "02505738-85a9-35ba-914d-cc67833ee938",
                        "target_lang_word": "existential",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "existential",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a88c3187-32c7-3355-bdd4-f25f6f1092eb",
                                        "entry_id": "9dbde7e0-af29-3e5a-b7d4-3a967db21a76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to existence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55f08a30-6063-3c1c-b9c5-05d02993eb93",
                                        "entry_id": "9dbde7e0-af29-3e5a-b7d4-3a967db21a76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Concerning the very existence of something, especially with regard to extinction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afa1a485-3c7e-4d41-808f-79a2edc79df8",
                                                "sense_id": "55f08a30-6063-3c1c-b9c5-05d02993eb93",
                                                "text": "existential risk"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "866e7b97-067d-4b1f-877b-9aa787d0c93f",
                                                "sense_id": "55f08a30-6063-3c1c-b9c5-05d02993eb93",
                                                "text": "Jaspers' main concern has been with existential dread, which he regards not as a symptom of mental illness, but as a result of rejecting religious faith. He proposes that man's only way out of existential dread is through a “leap into faith” which reconciles man with himself and with God, and provides an experience of the absolute which transcends mere sense experience."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "407e5d08-9346-4763-9212-aa037536249a",
                                                "sense_id": "55f08a30-6063-3c1c-b9c5-05d02993eb93",
                                                "text": "Here, therefore, we seek to assemble and assess the evidence to provide an overview of how serious trade is as an existential threat to avian taxa in Sundaic Indonesia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10b51e47-e297-42f7-8d04-9b6e2a85828e",
                                                "sense_id": "55f08a30-6063-3c1c-b9c5-05d02993eb93",
                                                "text": "To Musk, his vast fortune is a mere side effect of his ability not just to see but to do things others cannot, in arenas where the stakes are existential."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4bfda7b0-d573-3373-9fbb-08946d34d0ec",
                                        "entry_id": "9dbde7e0-af29-3e5a-b7d4-3a967db21a76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Based on experience; empirical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5aa71681-2f2a-4ea7-bf2e-1e815b283d73",
                                                "sense_id": "4bfda7b0-d573-3373-9fbb-08946d34d0ec",
                                                "text": "In recent books on logic, distinction is made between two orders of inquiry concerning anything. First, what is the nature of it? how did it come about? what is its constitution, origin, and history? And second, What is its importance, meaning, or significance, now that it is once here? The answer to the one question is given in an existential judgment or proposition. The answer to the other is a proposition of value, what the Germans call a Werthurtheil […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0f77602-48f2-3f67-8ecd-2da9a9feb2bc",
                                        "entry_id": "9dbde7e0-af29-3e5a-b7d4-3a967db21a76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to existentialism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f33cc95-aa4c-4045-991e-2588fac48056",
                                                "sense_id": "c0f77602-48f2-3f67-8ecd-2da9a9feb2bc",
                                                "text": "Some existential thinkers are concerned with artistic expression only indirectly, that is, they are passionately interested critics and analysts of art works."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43a5aad6-a9ba-3603-8049-62b341a5a672",
                                        "entry_id": "9dbde7e0-af29-3e5a-b7d4-3a967db21a76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to part of a clause that indicates existence, e.g. \\\"there is\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "existential",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f119aa37-4e37-36d8-9be8-72e486b38f8a",
                                        "entry_id": "64f529b0-1092-3a26-97ee-aefb454fde49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of existential clause."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16c50331-433c-4694-b0ee-6f3e844c66eb",
                                                "sense_id": "f119aa37-4e37-36d8-9be8-72e486b38f8a",
                                                "text": "We argue that existentials form a radial category, with a prototype and less canonical instances, where the prototype is clearly definable but the actual borderline between existentials and other clause types is fuzzy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7389c77-d76d-38e2-bfec-65f826baaa01",
                                        "entry_id": "64f529b0-1092-3a26-97ee-aefb454fde49",
                                        "glosses": [
